------------------------------------------------
|       MolSurf 1.0 - Build/Installation       |
------------------------------------------------
Alex R. -- arand@ices.utexas.edu -- 10/20/2010

To build:
$ cd $BUILD_DIR
$ cmake $SOURCE_DIR
$ make

BUILD_DIR - a location to place files generated during the build.
            It can be the same as the SOURCE_DIR
SOURCE_DIR - The location of the project's root CMakeLists.txt file.

The build process with produce the executable:

bin/MolSurf


Configuration options:

To build without CGAL or NFFT, use the cmake configuration
options which can be set with the ccmake command.

Note: Disabling CGAL will remove PocketTunnel functionality.
      Disabling NFFT will remove CoarseGrain functionality.  

